WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:19.050
let us face without panic the reality of our times&nbsp;
the fact that atom bombs may someday be dropped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:24.570
on our cities and let us prepare for survival&nbsp;
by understanding the weapon that threatens us

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:38.660
an atom bomb destroys or injures in three ways by&nbsp;
blast heat and radioactivity the blast of an atom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.300
bomb is its most important destructive agent in&nbsp;
Japan whole buildings were flattened by its force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.640
however many buildings of sturdy construction even&nbsp;
though close to the explosion remained standing

00:00:52.320 --> 00:01:00.780
the principal dangers of blasts are flying glass&nbsp;
and debris the fires it may start and the danger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:10.560
of being crushed in collapsing buildings the atom&nbsp;
bomb destroys by heat people caught in the open&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:17.280
as far as two miles away suffered flesh burns yet&nbsp;
protection could have been easily achieved here a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.490
bridge post and rail shielded the surface behind&nbsp;
it any solid material afforded similar protection

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.250
the third weapon of the bomb is radioactivity&nbsp;
thrown off at the instant of explosion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:38.290
however the majority of people exposed to&nbsp;
radiation recovered completely including a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:45.190
large percentage of those who suffered serious&nbsp;
radiation sickness today they lead normal lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:51.880
they bear children their children are normal&nbsp;
these then are the weapons of the atom bomb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.880 --> 00:02:00.250
that we must protect against blast heat and&nbsp;
radioactivity our cities are prime targets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:06.190
for atomic attack but mass evacuation would&nbsp;
be disastrous an enemy would like nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:11.770
better than to have us leave our cities empty&nbsp;
and unproductive if an emergency should come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:16.930
our factories will be battle stations&nbsp;
production must go on if we are to win

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.040
our officers and homes will also&nbsp;
be posted duty not to be deserted

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:32.280
with the knowledge of the first atomic explosions&nbsp;
to guide us our chances for survival will be far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.350
better than those of the people of Hiroshima&nbsp;
and Nagasaki if we act on our knowledge and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:46.020
are prepared the first job is to look over&nbsp;
your own home for shelter possibilities if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.020
you live in a private home that is well built&nbsp;
the cellar is the safest place to be the lower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.730
you get the more barriers there are likely&nbsp;
to be against blast heat and radioactivity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:03.660
select the basement wall nearest the probable&nbsp;
target area of your city if the house is blown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:09.450
over it will most likely fall away from this&nbsp;
wall if you have a workbench or strong table&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:14.400
big enough to get under move it into your&nbsp;
shelter area near a wall or strong supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.230
column if the time comes when you actually&nbsp;
have to take shelter lie under the table

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:30.110
if you live in a home that has no basement&nbsp;
choose a shelter area without windows on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:36.050
the ground floor an interior hallway is&nbsp;
probably best in time of emergency the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:39.980
shelter area should be cleared of mirrors&nbsp;
and other objects that might cause injury

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.120
if you lived in an apartment house&nbsp;
rules for taking shelter will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.930
posted in your building learn them also learn the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.530
location of public shelters in areas&nbsp;
where you work or frequently visited

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:05.490
there are many things you can begin doing right&nbsp;
now fireproof housekeeping is one so clean up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:15.900
that happy keep waste in covered containers&nbsp;
don't let trash pile up in the yard set aside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:22.170
a small supply of canned goods they're safe&nbsp;
from radioactivity have a good flashlight on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:31.890
hand electric lights may go out keep a first-aid&nbsp;
kit and learn how to stop bleeding make a habit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:38.340
of keeping a bottle of fresh water handy a&nbsp;
radio will be important for receiving vital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:45.390
instructions finally prepare the shelter area&nbsp;
and collect all necessary shelter equipment

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:58.520
in case of an actual raid or test drill the alert&nbsp;
will be a warbling siren blast lasting freedom

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.030
once you hear this act fast

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.150
pull down the shades or blinds&nbsp;
and close the drapes against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:31.770
flying glass turn off the burners of&nbsp;
your gas or electric stove disconnect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.130
any heating elements such as electric&nbsp;
irons hot plates or bathroom heaters

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:58.440
close all outside doors but leave them&nbsp;
unlocked turn off the gas or oil burners

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:26.240
taking shelter maybe a race against time&nbsp;
even when you have some advance warning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.400
but possibly there may be no time&nbsp;
an attack could come without warning

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:39.980
the sky would suddenly light up if the doorway&nbsp;
is right at hand use it if the nearest shelter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:44.270
is more than a couple of steps away fall&nbsp;
to the ground immediately flying glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.980
and debris or immediate danger so stay where&nbsp;
you are until you're sure it's safe to move

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:04.030
if you are at home when a surprise attack occurs&nbsp;
all beneath the table if it is very nearer or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:18.790
drop to the floor with your back to the window&nbsp;
the immediate danger is over in about a minute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:29.320
unless the explosion occurred near the ground&nbsp;
or water in this case radioactive materials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:33.820
are trapped in the particles of dirt or water&nbsp;
thrown up by the explosion when these particles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:38.410
fall back to earth they may be dangerous so&nbsp;
get indoors immediately after a ground-level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:48.010
explosion cover broken windows against radioactive&nbsp;
dust with blankets or cardboard civil-defense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:53.470
radiological teams equipped with radiation&nbsp;
survey meters will check on contamination in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.470 --> 00:08:00.940
any bombed area stay undercover until you hear&nbsp;
officially that it is safe outside if you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:07.660
been exposed to radioactive dust wash the exposed&nbsp;
areas pay particular attention to your hair get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:14.410
all the dirt from under your fingernails if the&nbsp;
people of Hiroshima and Nagasaki had known what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:21.010
we know about civil defense thousands of lives&nbsp;
would have been saved yes the knowledge is ours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:28.030
and preparation can mean survival for you so&nbsp;
act now someday your life may depend on it

